{"code":"import{z}from\"zod\";import{defineTool}from\"@papercusp/agent-mcp\";import{resolveAgentIdentity}from\"../coordination/identity\";import{COORD_ROLES}from\"../coordination/roles\";import{setClaimSpec}from\"../../scheduler/claim-spec-store\";var set_claim_spec_default=defineTool({name:\"scheduler:set_claim_spec\",profile:\"engineer\",description:\"Queen: set/replace a bee's versioned claim spec (view.filter + rank). The bee's scheduler:get_next then pulls deterministically per this spec within the global floors. Re-steer a running bee by setting a new spec (the revision bumps; the bee picks it up on its next get_next) \\u2014 not by micro-dispatching. Validates the spec; returns { ok, errors, revision }.\",guidance:{when:\"Handing work to a bee IS authoring its claim spec \\u2014 this is THE dispatch surface, not micro-dispatch. Encode a scoped VIEW (filter) + ORDERING (rank) over the work-item DAG: describe a LANE by property (plan/paths/tags/priority) for a standing, auto-inflowing, steal-able lane; reach for `id in [...]` ONLY to pin a fixed WAVE (hotfix/cutover/re-driving a known set \\u2014 it is STATIC: no auto-inflow, no work-stealing). The bee self-pulls via get_next within the global floors. Re-steer a running bee by setting a new spec (the revision bumps; it picks it up on its next get_next), never by re-dispatching.\",notWhen:\"Hand-picking each item for a bee (micro-dispatch) \\u2014 encode the policy in the spec instead. A spec that selects on `id` ALONE for a STANDING lane is hand-listing in disguise (recorded as an id-pin) \\u2014 write a property filter. Global hard floors (blocked/ready/dedup/cursed) cannot be set here \\u2014 the resolver always enforces them.\",chaining:\"scheduler:set_claim_spec (you) \\u2192 the bee's scheduler:get_next pulls per the spec.\"},capability:\"work_items:write\",requirePrincipal:false,agentRoles:[...COORD_ROLES],args:z.object({beeId:z.string().min(1).describe(\"the bee to steer (its session/owner id)\"),spec:z.